Abstract is a keyword which is used to define abstract classes and methods. The classes and methods with an abstract keyword are called concrete ones.
Abstract methods are those which are declared but don't have any implementation or logic while concrete methods have declaration and implementation or logic.
An abstract class can store both concrete and abstract methods, while a concrete class can store only concrete methods.
The object creation of an abstract class is not allowed because it contains incomplete methods which may result in runtime errors. 
These methods need to be inherit and override by providing an implementation by a concrete class in order to use them.
